<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>A bad omen? Syria bans women from university courses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3918fd2c0edb30fb440c5b9c7d06d3f98453a59600c256e6a475457a8f159ac6</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T20:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348--ba55f3eb7dc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The recent announcement that Syrian tertiary institutes will not allow women into some courses has triggered debate. Critics worry it may be a sign that the new Syrian government is restricting women's rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine may be involved in Mali's conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:988efd43528c2be9adf42912984d3ba19438ffb1d743016b3b776e40697c046e</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423--7ee87f683a22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Allegations that Ukrainian specialists are supporting Tuareg rebels in Mali highlight Kyiv's effort to challenge Russian influence far beyond the battlefield in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz heads to Asia as security issues loom large</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a42975ce424c1886ce8dd8828bdf850a88ac11c8559d0ab12570cea616117ad</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-heads-to-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065--83314a8603b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-heads-to-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz will be meeting the leaders of Singapore, Japan and South Korea as Germany seeks to adjust its foreign policy to rising uncertainty and threats to global supply chains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuelan opposition leader Machado returns from exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa73605bfa955abd6503389d0535b0f55e3425b01f4994f48a718ba0423d9bc3</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuelan-opposition-leader-machado-returns-from-exile/a-79759187--269b27174ea2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuelan-opposition-leader-machado-returns-from-exile/a-79759187?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nobel Peace Prize winner and popular Venezuelan political opposition figure Maria Corina Machado has returned after nearly a year away. Sitting President Rodriguez accused her of making a "show."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Protein shakes for teenagers: Good or bad idea?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:525a4ee77b0fe74fd6124d8c4c3f3e3ff6105724338aabfa0fe9fe32cebce253</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/protein-shakes-for-teenagers-good-or-bad-idea/a-79751929--869a08ab5ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protein-shakes-for-teenagers-good-or-bad-idea/a-79751929?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protein products are marketed as a way of building muscle and losing weight — and they're very popular with young people. They also claim to promote healthy growth in children. Is this true? How much protein is healthy?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda says it has no active Ebola cases, but infections in Kenya and Nigeria are prompting fresh scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d685135631a9f4ae57f7e36dca57f41c122968703c6045deed534d18977e7b9</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scr/a-79741580--819bf739b307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scrutiny/a-79741580?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Health officials are investigating whether Ebola patients in Kenya and Nigeria crossed paths at Uganda's main airport as conflicting accounts cloud the source of one infection.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot campaigns on Moroccan roots in challenge to Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b70b4fde068229e7ba35461f8e3d543a0c8c13fde3a1932dd703b5168fca2a7</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-campaigns-on-moroccan-roots-in-challenge-to-netanyahu/a-79747193--b8bf9b894fd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-campaigns-on-moroccan-roots-in-challenge-to-netanyahu/a-79747193?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israel prepares to vote, Gadi Eisenkot is leveraging his Moroccan heritage in Likud strongholds such as Sderot. From historical divides to October 7, identity and trauma are redefining the city's political loyalties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Prague honors Roma resistance fighters against Hitler</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6723fdf97545c3750e42904cbf5fa62cbe20d7520f7b8a567c5dff84319cf02</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015--c9d68b8992df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 1,400 Roma fought against the German Nazi occupation in Czechoslovakia. A new exhibition in Prague showcases the stories of partisans and soldiers whose fates barely received any attention for decades.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia looks to US for an AI edge as Yemen's Houthis up pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c3b63e8129967d331c96548cb95b63f6640684a53bc7cd3afd8bc66f0b0f3e6</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-looks-to-us-for-an-ai-edge-as-yemen-s-houthis-up-pressure/a-79735138--9b8ebc9e4129.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-looks-to-us-for-an-ai-edge-as-yemen-s-houthis-up-pressure/a-79735138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is helping Saudi Arabia fight the Houthi group in Yemen with AI-assisted targeting. But AI is not a magic bullet, experts say, and there are technological, political and human rights issues to consider.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Bulgaria, record low voter turnout triggers a November 1 presidential run-off in a poll colored by divisions over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3381034115d98df9775709b172e4590144d52bfdf2d5a8108c6bde715ebdc699</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by/a-79753496--78ae87f6d8b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Low voter turnout has triggered a run-off for the Bulgarian presidency. The vote was colored by strong divisions over Russia's war in Ukraine, and Sofia's relations with the Kremlin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
